menu "Agent Link StopWatch display"

    config AGENTLINK_DISPLAY_DIRECT_DMA
        bool "Push LVGL bands straight to the CO5300 by DMA (no PSRAM framebuffer)"
        default y
        help
            Each LVGL band is byte-swapped in place and sent to the panel with one asynchronous
            QSPI DMA transfer, so LVGL renders the next band while the previous one is on the wire.
            Off: the old path, which copies every band into a full-screen PSRAM framebuffer
            (M5GFX Panel_fb) and then pushes it to the panel line by line, synchronously.

    config AGENTLINK_DISPLAY_STATS
        bool "Log flush timing every 5 s"
        default n
        help
            Logs flushes, pixels, CPU time spent in the flush callback and time spent waiting
            for the previous DMA transfer (ESP_LOGI, tag sw-display).

    config AGENTLINK_DISPLAY_TE
        bool "Start each frame on the CO5300 tearing-effect pulse (experimental)"
        depends on AGENTLINK_DISPLAY_DIRECT_DMA
        default n
        help
            The panel pulses TE (G38) when its scan reaches line 466 (35h/44h in the init list).
            The first band of every refresh waits for that pulse (20 ms timeout) so the write
            starts in vertical blanking. Only areas that finish before the scan reaches them are
            tear-free; a full-screen redraw slower than one scan still tears, and the wait costs
            up to one frame (avg ~8 ms) per refresh. Three timeouts in a row turn it off.

endmenu

menu "Agent Link StopWatch I2C and touch"

    config AGENTLINK_I2C_FAST
        bool "Touch and RTC at 400 kHz I2C (fast mode)"
        default y
        help
            Runs the CST820 touch controller and the RX8130CE RTC at 400 kHz instead of 100 kHz,
            cutting a touch poll from ~1 ms to ~0.3 ms of bus time. Both datasheets allow 400 kHz,
            SYS_SDA/SCL have 2.2 kOhm pull-ups, and the M5IOE1 on the same bus already runs at
            400 kHz. The M5PM1 stays at its library default (100 kHz): it is read every 2 s only.

    config AGENTLINK_TOUCH_INT
        bool "Read the touch controller only after its INT line toggles"
        default y
        help
            The CST820 pulses TP_INT (G13) when it has a report. While no finger is down, a poll
            with no INT edge since the last read skips the I2C read; with a finger down every poll
            reads, as before. A read is still forced every 250 ms; if one of those finds a finger
            with no INT edge (twice), gating turns itself off until reboot.

endmenu
